"Superior Professor Worli Ro-den, called Joe, is the Artonan in charge of LeafSong's exam labs."
"He is abnormally tall and lanky, with so many tattoos he looks like a living circuit board."
"His tattoos mark him as a collector of contracts."
"He wears full wizard garb with pockets stuffed with food, and often skips lunch."
"A smart lens over one eye moves independently and serves as his System interface."
"He speaks flawless English and calls people darling, sweetheart and dear."
"To Alden Thorn he feels uneven, though less so than the Velras."
"He is a very harsh grader, inviting back only 5 of 75 examinees."
"Decades ago he sat on the committee that put the Hot Lab Coat in the Wardrobe."
"He took a grand senator's wife as his lover, and the authorities then punished his work."
"He is on parole, sentenced to teach at LeafSong after three decades away from teaching."
"For about sixteen years his lab on Moon Thegund contained demonic energies for rich patrons."
"That lab was confiscated and sold to the Yipalck Corporation."
"His System privileges to grant spell impressions or foundation points were revoked."
"He may pay only 500 Argold a day through his university account but can tip any amount himself."
"He sees Avowed as existential threats that make his species evolve."
"He keeps a bioweapon and a memory-altering serum ready, and prefers to shake dirtier hands."
"A couple of his human contractees are probably supervillains."
"He finds Earth's hero and villain dynamic absurd."
"He calls Alden's skill a limited edition gem, perfect for lab work."
"He traded Alden fifteen minutes of lessons for each trip to Thegund to fetch an assistant."
"He drew his half of that contract tattoo freehand on his shin."
"Alden's gremlin makes forming contracts with Alden harder for him."
"His wizard credit limit allows one round trip to Thegund per day."
"Loyalists from his old lab, two children among them, wait on Thegund to be carried out."
"That errand is illegal and could add about a decade to his sentence."
"He has a tattooed face, eats egg rolls, and carries many scalpels and a cigar case of vials."
"His office overlooks Hot Lab 7, which he calls a weapons lab; it holds a vat of eels."
"He poisoned the mishnen that bit off Stuart's foot."
"He holds contracts over nine students from the mishnen incident, to help overturn his sentence."
"He designed Alden's lab coat and loaned him a heavy ring that makes held things cling."
"He seems afraid of the Primary."
"He offered to hire Alden Thorn permanently in about a year."
"He refuses to teach Alden wizardry and strongly discourages him from studying it."
"He sent Alden with bombs for Thenn-ar to tidy up the Moon Thegund lab."
"He lived on Moon Thegund for years by choice, and his lab there doubled as his house."
"He gave Kibby eight lessons and had Instructor Gwen-lor record wizard lessons for her."
"He calls knighthood a terrible life for crazy wizards and idiots."
"He hid an auriad for Kibby inside her lesson cushion."
"Alis-art'h declined to prove he sabotaged his old Thegund lab."
"He prefers audio-only calls and has little funding left."
"Everyone believes he blew up his Thegund lab; he earns a small commission on the lab coat."
"Told that Thenn-ar had called him Ro, he went still and hung up."
"That autumn he was stripped of his Distinguished title and lost all summoning rights."
"He teaches labs Stuart attends and swears at students, though never at Alden or Stuart."
"In the Matadero flood Earth news called him the Bald General; he broke up the Bunker Street riot."
"He drained the Submerger contaminant by dropping marked objects, then summoning them back."
"His huge tawny auriad wraps his waist, and his embroidery shows mastery of seven magics."
"After the flood he declared a sharp break with Alden: future meetings will be empty pleasantries."
"He retracted Lesson One and told Alden to take the easy road for a few decades."
"He will formally hand Kibby to her new instructors after Thegund."
"At Matadero he lives on the top residential floor and always keeps a few Thegund grasshoppers."
"He told Alden to keep his old ring, or sell it or give it away."
"Stuart says he is obsessed with why nearly all Thegund bugs become demons."
"Yipalck was the largest backer of his research."
"Denied the title Trimeritorious, he destroyed a valuable invention and its records."
"He broke his assistants' secrecy contracts, though they could have fled to Chayklo any time."
"His scientists only had to agree to drop the research to leave Thegund, so his story was a lie."
"Late one night he met Alden at Matadero asking where he was going; Alden left without answering."
"He bedded Grand Senator Lamet-seepa's wife at a dinner party, suppressing her marriage contract."
"He claimed Thegund's Luklo region by heritage, infuriating the grand senators."
"His executioners placed him in a teaching post meant to make him yield."
